@start **The window opens on a single spine column.** Column 0, `phoU`, is carried by 100% of chromosomes, persistent, in a region of plasticity in 0% of calls {S1}. The model names 99% of them, at 0.04 bits {S1}.

@variable **The first fork is at `bglG`**, column 1, carried by 68%, the fewest named and most hesitant of its stretch {S2, S2.c1}. Then columns 15 to 17, `tnaB` to `tnaC`, are [[tryptophanase]] {S3, Q}. The most plastic stretch is column 30, `yidX`, in a region of plasticity in 78% of calls {S4, P}.

@model **The model names more genes on the spine columns than on the fork and variable ones**, 90 against 87%, and hesitates less there, 0.28 against 0.57 bits {M}. Its most hesitant column, 69, `yicJ`, is a fork column, at 1.26 bits {H}.

@end **The window ends in fork and variable columns.** Columns 68 to 79, `setC` to `ligB`, are carried by 19 to 71% of chromosomes {S14}. The last column is `ligB`, in 32% of chromosomes {E}.

@whole **Across the window it names 89% of genes**, 0.40 bits on average, perplexity 1.6 families {G}. Inside a region of plasticity it hesitates more than outside, 0.76 against 0.24 bits, and names fewer genes, 84% against 91% {C}.

